  "problem": "$$\n{y}^{\u2034}+{y}^{\u2032}=-{sec}^{3}\u2061(x),\\,{{y}_{1}=1,\\,{y}_{2}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x),\\,{y}_{3}=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x)}\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation and the set of fundamental solutions of the corresponding homogeneous equation above. \nUsing the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n$$\ny(x)=A+B\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x)+C\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x)+{u}_{1}(x)+{u}_{2}(x)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x)+{u}_{3}(x)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x).\n$$\n\nWhat is the function ${u}_{2}(x)?$",
